    <!--
        ISO 8583 field definition rules maintained by UIC:
        A   - Alphabetic, numeric or symbolic data aligned to the left and padded with spaces.
        N   - Numeric data aligned to the right and padded with zeroes. Amount fields use the two
              least significant digits as decimals when encoded as packed BCD.
        H   - Binary data represented as hexadecimal characters without transformation.
        ..  - Variable length field where the length indicator occupies one byte.
        ... - Variable length field where the length indicator occupies two bytes.

        lenType - Encoding for the length indicator (ASC, HEX or BCD). Defaults to BCD when omitted.
        align   - Alignment strategy for fixed length fields (LEFT or RIGHT).
        padding - Hexadecimal byte used to pad fixed length values when the provided data is shorter
                  than the configured maximum.
    -->

